<title>UK: Laird sells belt unit to Svedala.</title>
<headline>Laird sells belt unit to Svedala.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British-based Laird Group Plc said on Monday it had sold its Cable Belt long-distance conveyor belt manufacturing unit to Sweden's Svedala Industri AB, for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>In a statement Laird said the deal would allow the group to further focus on its core business.</p>
<p>Cable Belt has about 80 employees and had 1996 turnover of 12.5 million stg from net assets of less than 2.0 million stg.</p>
<p>Svedala is a leading manufacturer of equipment and systems for construction, mineral processing and materials handling.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44-171 542 7717</p>
</text>
